From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:45:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: arm-smmu-qcom: keep AFE disabled on MSM8226

MSM8226 GPU short-descriptor contexts fault with FSR.AFF when SCTLR.AFE
is enabled, despite valid AP0 bits in the second-level descriptors.
The ring is consumed without executing commands and submission fences
never complete. Hardware address-translation tests on SM-T531 fail with
AFE set and resolve the expected physical address when only AFE is cleared.
A glmark2 scene then completes through Mesa Freedreno.

Keep AFE clear in the existing MSM8226 implementation callback. This
matches the vendor short-descriptor setup and retains full AP permission
checking. Leave the other SMMU variants unchanged.

Reference: LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_msm8226 commit
3fa1853ed5d6c3a8ef5a2fda9822705243bbc256, drivers/iommu/msm_iommu-v1.c,
__program_context().

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -713,8 +713,17 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void qcom_msm8226_smmu_write_sctlr(struct arm_smmu_device *smmu,
+					int idx, u32 val)
+{
+	/* Use full AP permissions, as in the MSM8226 vendor implementation. */
+	arm_smmu_cb_write(smmu, idx, ARM_SMMU_CB_SCTLR,
+			  val & ~ARM_SMMU_SCTLR_AFE);
+}
+
 static const struct arm_smmu_impl qcom_msm8226_smmu_impl = {
 	.cfg_probe = qcom_msm8226_smmu_cfg_probe,
+	.write_sctlr = qcom_msm8226_smmu_write_sctlr,
 };
 
 static const struct qcom_smmu_match_data msm8226_smmu_data = {
